    "content": "The file contained exactly **400** instances of `9` \u2014 so the second operand is a 400-digit number: 10\u2074\u2070\u2070 \u2212 1. That's why `add` rejected it: it exceeds the largest value a standard floating-point number can hold (~1.8\u00d710\u00b3\u2070\u2078), so no decomposition into float-sized chunks can represent it either.\n\nThe exact math: 12345.678 + (10\u2074\u2070\u2070 \u2212 1) = 10\u2074\u2070\u2070 + 12344.678. Let me verify this carry pattern with the `add` tool on identical smaller-scale cases:",
